---@class posthog.canvases.GetCanvasesStateRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this canvas.
---@field cursor? string Cursor from next_cursor. Resumes after the last entry of the previous page, so an entry that exists for the whole read comes back exactly once. A key written between pages can be missing. Keep filters unchanged between pages. Takes precedence over offset.
---@field key? string Only read this exact key.
---@field key_prefix? string Only read entries whose key starts with this prefix.
---@field keys_only? boolean True returns a key inventory without stored values.
---@field limit? number Maximum entries per page. Omit for the full state. Prefer an inventory and state/value for large values.
---@field offset? number Entry offset from next_offset. Keep filters unchanged between pages. Prefer cursor: an offset can skip or repeat entries when state changes between pages.
---@field scope? posthog.canvases.GetCanvasesStateRequestScope|string Only read this scope. * `user` - user * `shared` - shared

---@alias posthog.canvases.GetCanvasesStateRequestScope "user"|"shared"

---@class posthog.canvases.GetCanvasesStateValueRequest
